==========================================================================================
ROOT CAUSE OF THE iOS/macOS COMPILE FAILURES (pre-existing, outside allowed files)
==========================================================================================
Shared component Sources/Components/UI/Cards.swift declares:
    public struct TSGlassPanel<Content: View>: View {
        private let content: () -> Content
        public init(@ViewBuilder content: @escaping () -> Content) { ... }   // ESCAPING
    }
Multiple sibling AI* surfaces wrap it in a NON-escaping helper, e.g.:
    private func glass(@ViewBuilder _ content: () -> some View) -> some View {
        TSGlassPanel { content() }   // captures non-escaping `content` in escaping closure
    }
On Swift 6.3.2 this is a deterministic "escaping closure captures non-escaping parameter"
error. The fix belongs in those sibling files (mark the helper param @escaping) or the
shared component — BOTH outside this prompt's allowed files (Toast.*). The Toast surface
deliberately does NOT use TSGlassPanel (it uses TSCard + token-driven backgrounds), so it
is immune and compiles cleanly.

